### Root of the OL state.
###
### From V1 on, the protocol state root that block headers, checkpoints, and
### genesis commit to is the hash tree root of this container, over exactly
### these three fields. Under V0, the 0.3.0 rules, the protocol state root is
### the bare `chainstate_root` and this container is not committed. Its layout
### never changes; a new chainstate layout changes only what `chainstate_root`
### commits to.
###
### The version fields are raw integers rather than `OLSpecId`, whose decoding
### rejects unknown values. The current spec must be known, since it selects the
### chainstate layout; the staged version is kept as a raw value, so the state
### decodes whatever it holds. They are `uint32` for headroom, since this layout
### never changes; for any value below 256 a `uint32` field has the same hash
### tree root as a `uint8` one.
class OLRootState(Container):
    ### Spec the chainstate was produced under.
    ###
    ### Selects the chainstate layout through the spec-to-layout mapping.
    cur_spec_version: uint32

    ### Spec the state stages for the next epoch.
    ###
    ### No rule set stages a spec, so in every state the rules produce this
    ### equals `cur_spec_version`. Nodes select the next epoch's spec from the
    ### L1 manifests the epoch processed instead.
    staged_spec_version: uint32

    ### Hash tree root of the chainstate in the layout `cur_spec_version` maps to.
    chainstate_root: Bytes32
